{
  "title": "ToDLPack Speed Regression",
  "issue_id": "162113",
  "bug_description": "### 🐛 Describe the bug\n\nPreviously in https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/83069, the toDLPack converter introduces a normalization step that changes the strides to 1 when shape[i] == 1\n\nThis step, however, calls as_strided during toDLPack, and can slow down the toDLPack about 3x. This causes PyTorch's DLPack conversion to be around 0.6 us overhead per call from the < 0.2us.\n\nMost of the framework handles toDLPack conversion around 0.1 - 0.2 us level, which helps to have good normal eager mode conversion with torch\n\n\ncc @msaroufim @jerryzh168",
  "apis": [
    "torch"
  ],
  "best_code": "",
  "pull_urls": [
    "https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/83158",
